      <memberdef kind="function" id="minunit_8h_1ab26e74f6c5baa9a0f2629d3f89aa62bb" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>static void mu_assert</definition>
        <argsstring>(const char *file, int line, const char *msg, int expr)</argsstring>
        <name>mu_assert</name>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>file</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>line</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>msg</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>expr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Generic boolean assertion.</para>
<para>Evaluates <emphasis>expr</emphasis>. Prints a green <bold>PASS</bold> line on success, or a red <bold>FAIL</bold> line including the source location on failure. Do not call directly — use the <emphasis>MU_ASSERT</emphasis> macro.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>msg</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Human-readable description shown in the output line. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>expr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Non-zero = pass, zero = fail.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Example:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="normal">MU_ASSERT(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;pointer<sp/>is<sp/>not<sp/>null&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>ptr<sp/>!=<sp/>NULL);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="minunit.h" line="83" column="19" bodyfile="minunit.h" bodystart="83" bodyend="96"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="minunit_8h_1a7197018c003e82f9dcd0f5dc9d42e431" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>static void mu_assert_int</definition>
        <argsstring>(const char *file, int line, int expected, int actual)</argsstring>
        <name>mu_assert_int</name>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>file</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>line</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>expected</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>actual</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Integer equality assertion.</para>
<para>Compares <emphasis>expected</emphasis> and <emphasis>actual</emphasis> as <computeroutput>int</computeroutput> values. On failure the output includes both the expected and the actual values. Do not call directly — use the <emphasis>MU_ASSERT_INT</emphasis> macro.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The value the expression should produce. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>actual</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The expression under test.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Example:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="normal">MU_ASSERT_INT(3,<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal">)ft_lstsize(list));</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="minunit.h" line="118" column="19" bodyfile="minunit.h" bodystart="118" bodyend="132"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="minunit_8h_1a3576f9c0f7a95faf2e3e2deff0c3291d" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>static void mu_assert_str</definition>
        <argsstring>(const char *file, int line, const char *msg, const char *expected, const char *actual)</argsstring>
        <name>mu_assert_str</name>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>file</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>line</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>msg</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>expected</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>actual</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>String equality assertion (NULL-safe).</para>
<para>Compares <emphasis>expected</emphasis> and <emphasis>actual</emphasis> with strcmp(3). A NULL <emphasis>actual</emphasis> is treated as a failure and printed as <computeroutput>&quot;(null)&quot;</computeroutput> in the output line. Do not call directly — use the <emphasis>MU_ASSERT_STR</emphasis> macro.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>msg</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Human-readable label shown in the output line. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The expected C string (must not be NULL). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>actual</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The actual C string returned by the code under test.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Example:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="normal">MU_ASSERT_STR(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;newest<sp/>entry&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;pwd&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>history_prev(&amp;h));</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
