      <memberdef kind="function" id="minunit_8h_1a3d2c36d46d4c778dc62e61dda3bce3e8" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>static void mu_run</definition>
        <argsstring>(const char *name, void(*fn)(void))</argsstring>
        <name>mu_run</name>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>name</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>void(*)(void)</type>
          <declname>fn</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Execute a test suite function and announce its name.</para>
<para>Prints a cyan header line with the name of <emphasis>fn</emphasis> then calls <computeroutput>fn()</computeroutput>. Typically used in <computeroutput>main()</computeroutput> of <ref refid="test__runner_8c" kindref="compound">test_runner.c</ref>. Do not call directly — use the <emphasis>MU_RUN</emphasis> macro.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>name</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Stringified name of the test suite function. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fn</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Function pointer to the test suite.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Example:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="normal">MU_RUN(<ref refid="test__list_8c_1ad88047b8cb23d2d51d9b331a013b922f" kindref="member">test_list_suite</ref>);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="minunit.h" line="192" column="19" bodyfile="minunit.h" bodystart="192" bodyend="196"/>
